From 6d3133df46b7f79e29dad8abaeb7b2fc07ff83ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:41:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 58/60] Clear stale "in progress" on idle CLI agents

A CLI agent session is registered as InProgress when its command is
detected and only left that state on Stop/StopFailure or Ctrl-C. A freshly
started or resumed Claude waiting for its first prompt, and a turn the user
interrupted with Esc (Claude Code fires no hook for that), kept showing
"in progress" in the vertical tabs and the Agents panel. SessionStart now
marks the session idle, and IdlePrompt ends a turn still marked InProgress
as Cancelled. Both change the status quietly so they don't notify like a
finished task.

Also restores the compute_valid_paths test helper the link-detection tests
use, which the host path resolution change removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
